            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> With the recent consolidation of feature requests being tied to this change notification, that means that every active capability/feature was also firing every debounce interval instead of being debounced until changes settled.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure why that is a problem?\r\n\r\n> Even when coming back from idle, a change is likely to be followed by more changes\r\n\r\nDepends on what kind of edits one is making. With the motion based edits there's a good chance that single edits followed by idle (moving cursor) does happen.\r\n\r\nWas there an issue that motiviated this? I'd think this might be sacrificing responsiveness for fast servers while maybe gaining some reduced load for slower servers?",
